                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Political groups and aspiring presidential candidates are working overtime to mislead the public about commonsense government reforms in the new budget. That includes Josh Shapiro, who recently claimed that tens of thousands of local residents would lose SNAP coverage. \n\nHere\u2019s the truth: SNAP \u2014 which is administered by the states with federal dollars \u2014 is plagued by waste because of a lack of accountability for errors. For example, Pennsylvania has seen error rates as high as 16% in recent years. This budget makes a commonsense change: when error rates are high, states will pay a portion of the cost. When they\u2019re low, they will continue to pay nothing. It\u2019s up to Governor Shapiro to take accountability for waste, protect taxpayer dollars, and safeguard federal funding.",
